---
import FrameworkLayout from '@/layouts/FrameworkLayout.astro';
---

<FrameworkLayout
  title="4-O Framework | ChiroCandy"
  description="The 4-O Framework outlines four outcomes for chiropractic practice growth: Online visibility, Offers that convert, Operations that retain, and Outcomes that drive referrals."
  slug="4-o-framework"
  heroTitle="4-O Framework"
  heroAnswer="The 4-O Framework is ChiroCandy's four-pillar model for sustainable chiropractic growth. You win Online, convert with strong Offers, retain through Operations, then grow through patient Outcomes and referrals."
  definition="A practice growth checklist that connects marketing, front desk, clinical experience, and referral systems into four measurable outcomes."
  stages={[
    {
      title: 'What does Online mean in the 4-O Framework?',
      answer:
        'Online is your visibility layer: search rankings, ads, social presence, and a website that loads fast and answers patient questions.',
      detail:
        'If prospects cannot find you or understand your offer in under a minute, nothing downstream matters. Online covers SEO, paid traffic, reviews visible in search, and mobile-friendly pages.',
    },
    {
      title: 'How do Offers and Operations turn leads into loyal patients?',
      answer:
        'Offers give prospects a clear reason to book now. Operations keep them showing up, paying, and staying in care.',
      detail:
        'A strong offer names the problem, states what they get, and removes friction at checkout. Operations covers phone answer speed, scheduling, reminders, and follow-up. Marketing fills the calendar, but weak offers or sloppy front desk leak the growth Online created.',
    },
    {
      title: 'What Outcomes turn patients into referral sources?',
      answer:
        'Outcomes are the clinical and service results patients feel, plus the systems that ask for reviews and referrals at the right moment.',
      detail:
        'When patients get better and feel cared for, they tell others. Outcomes also include tracking satisfaction, collecting testimonials, and reactivation for patients who drifted. Referrals are the cheapest growth channel when Online, Offers, and Operations work together.',
    },
  ]}
  faqs={[
    {
      question: 'Which O should a struggling practice fix first?',
      answer:
        'Start with Online if nobody is finding you, Offers if traffic does not convert, or Operations if leads book but do not stay. Outcomes compound once the other three are solid.',
    },
    {
      question: 'Can the 4-O Framework work for a new practice?',
      answer:
        'Yes. New practices often over-invest in Online while neglecting Offer clarity and Operations. Running all four in order prevents filling a leaky bucket.',
    },
  ]}
  relatedServices={[
    { href: '/services/web-design/', label: 'Chiropractic Web Design' },
    { href: '/services/reactivation-campaigns/', label: 'Patient Reactivation' },
    { href: '/services/search-engine-optimization/', label: 'SEO for Chiropractors' },
  ]}
/>
